Since \(\mathbf E\perp \mathbf v\), we also have
\[
\mathbf B=\frac{1}{c^2}\mathbf v\times \mathbf E,
\qquad
u=\frac{\epsilon_0E^2}{2}+\frac{B^2}{2\mu_0}
=\frac{\epsilon_0E^2}{2}\left(1+\frac{v^2}{c^2}\right),
\qquad
\mathbf g=\epsilon_0\mathbf E\times\mathbf B
=\frac{\epsilon_0E^2}{c^2}\mathbf v .
\]

